Welcome to Voyager 3.5.2, a restoration of VaporWare's Voyager V3
for classic 68k Amiga.

Oliver Wagner started Voyager in 1995. David Gerber co-developed
it with him. The last boxed commercial product was Voyager 3.2
(16.4.2000). A limited 3.3 alpha / public-beta line followed
(from August 2000): new layout engine and window framework,
vertical nav panel, optional TearOff, CManager aliases in the
URL gadget, ftp. auto-prefix, HTML on HTTP 4xx/5xx, AS225
removed. Public betas 3.3.65 and 3.3.75; 3.3.126 (27.12.2002)
for 68k and MorphOS, followed with alpha releases. Printing
and some layout/JS gaps remained. A short 3.4 CVS series
followed. Source to a 3.4 release was later published under 
the GNU GPL. This 3.5.2 build is that GPL tree made usable.

Requirements: MUI, a TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library). AmiTLS
(LIBS:amitls.library) and Certificates/cacert.pem for HTTPS.
cybergraphics.library is used when present for RTG.

Runtime vapor_toolkit.library dependencies and keyfile checks are 
removed in this Free and Open Source release.


See Docs/Readme.Docs and Docs/voyager3docs/main.html in this
drawer (factory fastlink Docs). README.md / CHANGELOG.md are
in the source tree:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  http://www.amigazen.com/voyager/
  voyager@amigazen.com

------------------------------------------------------------

Newsflash: 3.5.2 compared with a 3.2 binary install

* SAS/C 68k smakefile for V, imgdecode, MimePrefs, libmath64

* Image decoder linked into the executable; cybergraphics.library
  pixel-write paths

* SpeedBar toolbar enabled; TearOff panels disabled

* No vapor_toolkit.library / keyfile; GPL, no registration nag

* HTTPS via AmiTLS (TLS 1.2, SNI). OpenSSL 0.9 VSSL is not
  linked. 

* Default User-Agent uses Firefox 4 grammar with AmigaVoyager
  in the Mozilla comment so current CDNs do not reject the
  client. The Spoof menu can still identify as Voyager.

* Compile, layout, image, HTTP header, and first-paint fixes
  required to run at all

The per-version history for the limited 3.4/3.3 line and for
Voyager 3.2 and older (3.0.0 through 3.2) is in CHANGELOG.md
in the source tree. The 3.3.0-3.3.127 build log is Source/V.ReadMe:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md

Dead VaporWare URLs (v3.vapor.com, bugs.vapor.com, mailing lists) no
longer apply. Historical notes: https://zapek.com/software/voyager/


Support & Bug reporting
=======================

For 3.5.2, use GitHub or email. The VaporWare bug tracker and
mailing list are gone.

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  voyager@amigazen.com

JSERROR.LOG in the program drawer is still useful for JS
quirks when that preference is enabled.

Credits
=======

Voyager is (C) 1995-2003 by Oliver Wagner, David Gerber,
Jon Bright, Matt Sealey, and the VaporWare Voyager team.
Released under the GNU GPL v3.

V3 was a joint effort conducted by several people
using the powers of CVS:

The flash player and many many core changes have been done
by David "Zapek" Gerber <zapek@vapor.com>

The new bookmark and toolbar system has been devised by the wits
of Simone "Wiz" Tellini <wiz@vapor.com>

Jerome "KingGuppy" Fisher <kingguppy@vapor.com> contributed
the new Textinput functionality including HTML tag highliting.
He also squashed some bugs.

The GUI cleanup and the new about:, plus the Voyager
Portal site (http://v3.vapor.com) design are done by
Ben "Beej" Preece <beej@vapor.com>

The nifty new V3 logo is done by Jason "Morden" Murray
<morden@sub.net.au>, who also did the www.vapor.com web
site design.

The Vpdf plugin was done by Emmanuel Lesueur
<lesueur@club-internet.fr>.

3.5.2 restoration: amigazen project. AmiTLS / BearSSL as the
shipping VSSL backend. The original authors are not affiliated
with amigazen project.

Voyager V3 is dedicated to the memory of Oliver Wagner,
1969-2016.
